urce":{"worldId":"ac","uuid":null,"coreVersion":"0.8.8","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"2.6.0.6437"},"coreVersion":"14.363","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.1.2","lastModifiedBy":"TWU0FLEEJw1nn2KO","createdTime":1780421721561,"modifiedTime":1780421721561},"_id":"CYECNDrPLhztAlIr","ownership":{"default":0}},{"name":"Animal Companion","type":"class","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/class.svg","effects":[],"flags":{"core":{},"pf2e":{"grantedBy":{"id":"CYECNDrPLhztAlIr","onDelete":"cascade"}}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The following are the base statistics for a young animal companion, the first animal companion most characters get. You adjust these statistics depending on the type of animal you choose. Animal companions calculate their modifiers and DCs just as you do with one difference: the only item bonuses they can benefit from are to Speed and AC (their maximum item bonus to AC is +3). As you gain levels, you might be able to make your companion stronger by advancing it.</p><p>An animal companion's starting statistics are as follows.</p><ul><li><strong>Level:</strong> Your animal companion's level is equal to yours.</li><li><strong>Proficiencies:</strong> Your animal companion is trained in its unarmed attacks, unarmored defense, barding (a type of armor for animals), all saving throws, Perception, Acrobatics, and Athletics. Animal companions can't use abilities that require greater Intelligence, such as @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.tHCqgwjtQtzNqVvd]{Coerce} or Decipher Writing, even if trained in the appropriate skill, unless they have a specialization that allows it.</li><li><strong>Attribute Modifiers:</strong> An animal companion begins with base attribute modifiers listed in its stat block.</li><li><strong>Hit Points:</strong> Your animal companion has ancestry Hit Points from its type, plus a number of Hit Points equal to 6 plus its Constitution modifier for each level you have.</li></ul>"},"rules":[{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"override","path":"flags.pf2e.disableABP","value":true,"priority":10},{"key":"ActorTraits","add":["minion"]},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"upgrade","path":"system.proficiencies.defenses.light-barding.rank","priority":41,"value":1},{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"upgrade","path":"system.proficiencies.defenses.heavy-barding.rank","priority":41,"value":1},{"key":"AdjustModifier","predicate":["bonus:type:item"],"selectors":["attack","damage","skill-check","saving-throw"],"suppress":true},{"key":"AdjustModifier","predicate":["bonus:type:item"],"selectors":["ac"],"mode":"downgrade","value":3}],"slug":"animal-companion","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":{"schema":0.955,"foundry":"14.363","system":"8.1.2"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"keyAbility":{"value":[],"selected":null},"items":{},"hp":6,"trainedSkills":{"value":["acrobatics","athletics"],"additional":0},"perception":1,"savingThrows":{"fortitude":1,"reflex":1,"will":1},"attacks":{"simple":0,"martial":0,"advanced":0,"unarmed":1,"other":{"name":"","rank":0}},"defenses":{"unarmored":1,"light":0,"medium":0,"heavy":0},"spellcasting":0,"ancestryFeatLevels":{"value":[]},"classFeatLevels":{"value":[]},"generalFeatLevels":{"value":[]},"skillFeatLevels":{"value":[]},"skillIncreaseLevels":{"value":[]}},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.AC-Features.Item.KKOgokqHa7RjVDN6","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":{"worldId":"ac","uuid":null,"coreVersion":"0.8.8","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"2.6.0.6437"},"coreVersion":"14.363","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.1.2","lastModifiedBy":"TWU0FLEEJw1nn2KO","createdTime":1780421721561,"modifiedTime":1780421721561},"folder":null,"sort":3600000,"_id":"HJM42g9xbYP1Lw72","ownership":{"default":0}},{"name":"Horse Support Benefit","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":8400000,"flags":{"core":{},"pf2e":{"grantedBy":{"id":"CYECNDrPLhztAlIr","onDelete":"cascade"}}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>Until the start of your next turn, if you're mounted on your horse and moved 10 feet or more on the action before a melee Strike, add a circumstance bonus to damage for that Strike equal to twice the number of weapon damage dice. If your weapon already has the jousting weapon trait, increase the trait's damage bonus by 2 per die instead.</p><p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.AC-effects.Item.xe5pfyTYOWMYG1T8]{Effect: Horse Support Benefit}</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"horse-support-benefit","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":{"schema":0.955,"foundry":"14.363","system":"8.1.2"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":1},"deathNote":false},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.AC-Support.Item.wf20kx6pPGBWwUn2","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"14.363","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.1.2","lastModifiedBy":"TWU0FLEEJw1nn2KO","createdTime":1780421721561,"modifiedTime":1780421721561},"_id":"XbJaM1Nwilx1uOw3","ownership":{"default":0}},{"folder":"xW9aBqaSBpQRX72n","name":"Scourge Infection","type":"effect","effects":[],"system":{"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":{"schema":0.955,"foundry":"14.363","system":"8.1.2"}},"description":{"value":"<p>It's in your blood…</p>","gm":"<h1><strong>IF YOU ARE A GM READING THIS DO </strong><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">NOT</span></strong></span><strong> REMOVE THIS EFFECT FROM A PLAYER CHARACTER!</strong></h1><p><em>GM Note: Scourge Infection is </em><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><em><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">level 24,</span></em></span><em> it is listed as level 0 in this effect to prevent metagaming as a failsafe if a player finds the effect in the compendium.</em></p><p></p><p><em>This effect exists on tokens specifically for GMs. Players are not able to see it, including the icon on their token. Players should not be able to see the effect ever, don't uncheck the 'Unidentified?' box or click the eye icon on the effects tab of the character's sheet.</em></p><hr><p><em><strong>Saving Throw: </strong>Varies <strong>Onset: </strong>2 minutes</em></p><p><em><strong>Special: </strong>A creature cannot recover from the first two stages of Scourge infection on its own. They must be assisted by another creature via @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.TC7OcDa7JlWbqMaN]{Treat Disease}. When a creature does so, the infected creature immediately attempts a Will save with a DC equal to the very-hard difficulty DC for their level. On a success, the infected creature must then attempt a Foritude save with a DC equal to the very-hard difficulty DC for their level. On a success, the infected creature's Scourge infection stage is reduced by 1, but Scourge remains in their body (Carrier, Stage 0). Being reexposed to Scourge later causes the formerly infected creature to skip the onset stage of the infection.</em></p><p><em><strong>Stage 1: (1 day, disease) </strong>Scourge hides under the creature's skin, observing. The infection can usually be visually identified by a red outline of the creature's sclera. Whenever a creature infected with Scourge attempts an action that would harm another Scourged creature or otherwise disrupt Scourge itself, they must attempt a @Check[flat|dc:3], disrupting the action on a failure.</em></p><p><em><strong>Stage 2: (1 month, disease) </strong>Scourge takes a greater hold on the body of the creature it is infecting, causing its blood to become viscous with the consistency of honey. The DC to have an action disrupted from stage 1 of the infection increases to a @Check[flat|dc:8]. Additionally, the creature gains resistance to bleeding damage equal to half its level. When the infected creature dies, a Scourgespawn with a level closest to the creature's level erupts from the creature's corpse after one round.</em></p><hr><p><em>After the duration of stage 2 has passed, the infection remains at stage 2 until activated by Scourge itself, a Scourge Nexus, or another exceptionally powerful Scourged creature. When activated, the infected creature becomes immune to effects that would activate its infection for 24 hours.</em></p><hr><p><em><strong>Stage 3: (until activated, posession) </strong>Scourge begins assimilating the infected creature into the hivemind. The infection loses the disease trait and gains the possession trait. Treat Disease is no longer an applicable method of reducing the stage of the infection, which must be removed via a method of expelling a creature possessing another creature. If the infection would be removed from the infected creature (such as the effects of an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.6llILJtsTPgtYXgx]{Astral} rune), the infection's stage is reduced by 1, rather than expelling Scourge entirely. If the method of removing the posession requires a save, use the infected creature's saving throw modifier, if the effect requires a counteract check, use Scourge's level as the counteract level (24). The creature gains weakness equal to their level to Siccatite and Time. The DC to have an action disrupted from stage 1 of the infection increases to a @Check[flat|dc:13]. The resistance to bleeding damage gained from stage 2 of the infection increases to the infected creature's level. Whenever the posessed creature starts their turn, they must attempt a @Check[flat|dc:16]. On a failure, they are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9qGBRpbX9NEwtAAr]{Controlled} by Scourge for their first action for that turn, or their first two actions on a critical failure.</em></p><p><em><strong>Stage 4: (until activated, posession) </strong>The infected creature fully succumbs to the infection, becoming part of Scourge itself. The infected creature becomes immune to bleeding, and becomes permanently @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9qGBRpbX9NEwtAAr]{Controlled} by Scourge until the infection's stage is reduced.</em></p>"},"publication":{"title":"The Moonlit March","authors":"Spats","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"rules":[{"key":"Resistance","type":"bleed","value":"@actor.level/2","predicate":["parent:badge:value:3"]},{"key":"Resistance","type":"bleed","value":"@actor.level","predicate":["parent:badge:value:4"]},{"key":"Weakness","type":["siccatite","time"],"value":"@actor.level","predicate":[{"gte":["parent:badge:value",4]}]},{"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.9qGBRpbX9NEwtAAr","predicate":["parent:badge:value:5"],"onDeleteActions":{"grantee":"restrict"},"inMemoryOnly":true},{"key":"Immunity","type":"bleed","predicate":["parent:badge:value:5"]}],"slug":"scourge-infection","traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"level":{"value":0},"duration":{"value":-1,"unit":"unlimited","expiry":null,"sustained":false},"tokenIcon":{"show":true},"unidentified":true,"start":{"value":38268,"initiative":0},"badge":{"type":"counter","value":1,"labels":["Carrier","Stage 1","Stage 2","Stage 3","Stage 4"],"loop":false,"min":null,"max":null},"fromSpell":false,"context":{"origin":{"actor":"Scene.haAPUqMP9Vyq9aKe.Token.tSPli0wJr3PZV48A.Actor.H1PFteg1nGVoGGoY","token":"Scene.haAPUqMP9Vyq9aKe.Token.tSPli0wJr3PZV48A","item":"Scene.haAPUqMP9Vyq9aKe.Token.tSPli0wJr3PZV48A.Actor.H1PFteg1nGVoGGoY.Item.RpligwhxDpTrs8Pk","spellcasting":null,"rollOptions":[]},"target":null,"roll":null}},"img":"modules/the-moonlit-march-module/ART/OTHER/orb-swirling-red.webp","sort":200000,"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.the-moonlit-march-module.items.Item.UTMwx2FT7R44pQCA","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"14.363","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.1.2","lastModifiedBy":"TWU0FLEEJw1nn2KO","cre